      "text": "## U.S. ARMY PREPARING FOR MASS CASUALTIES, CONTESTED SKIES & BATTLEFIELD BURIALS — ANOTHER MAJOR EVENT NARRATIVE SEEDING DEVELOPMENT\n\nAdd OPERATION DRAGON COVENANT to the list....\n\nOn October 20–21, the Army conducted an extraordinary exercise at Fort Bragg, preparing for large-scale warfare where American forces may no longer control the skies.\n\nThe exercise included something particularly significant:\n\nTemporary battlefield burial operations on a scale not experienced since the Korean War.\n\nOn October 26, the Army announced its findings.\n\nHERE'S WHAT THE MILITARY REVEALED:\n\n🔴 FIRST SINCE KOREA: Preparing for large-scale temporary battlefield burials, not conducted at this scale since the 1950–1953 conflict.\n\n🔴 2,400 REMAINS PER DAY: An engineer company with eight bulldozers and four excavators could prepare and close burial trenches for up to 2,400 fallen personnel in 24 hours.\n\n🔴 MASS BURIAL TRENCHES: D6 bulldozers excavated trenches accommodating 20 remains each, averaging 75 minutes per trench.\n\n🔴 130 RELIGIOUS SUPPORT PERSONNEL: Chaplains trained for scenarios where individual funerals become impossible during continuous mass-casualty operations.\n\n🔴 PRESERVATION & EXHUMATION: Simulated remains were buried and recovered to test preservation for future identification and repatriation.\n\n🔴 PSYCHOLOGICAL STRAIN: Religious support teams could experience exhaustion within four to six hours.\n\n🔴 MORE TRAINING COMING: Spring 2027 exercises will include nighttime blackouts, security teams, medical facilities, and mortuary collection points.\n\nSgt. 1st Class Delbert Ruede made a revealing statement:\n\n\"If we went to war tomorrow, we would be making this up as we went along.\"\n\nFor decades, American forces relied on air superiority and rapid casualty evacuation.\n\nNow the Army is preparing for a battlefield where neither can be guaranteed.\n\nTHE MAJOR EVENT NARRATIVE SEEDING TIMELINE\n\nFor months, we've documented an accumulation of warnings, military preparations, and news coverage involving extraordinary disruption.\n\n🔴 CYBERATTACKS: Growing coverage of cyber intrusions, infrastructure vulnerabilities, and threats to power and communications.\n\n🔴 GLOBAL PREPAREDNESS: Multiple governments urging citizens to stockpile food, water, and emergency supplies.\n\n🔴 HOMELAND DEFENSE: Increased military readiness and critical infrastructure protection.\n\n🔴 ELECTION CYBERSECURITY: Attempted intrusions targeting election-related systems and expanded military cybersecurity discussions ahead of November 3.\n\n🔴 NUCLEAR & ENERGY SECURITY: Nuclear deterrence, energy infrastructure protection, and potential great-power escalation.\n\n🔴 DRAGON COVENANT: Preparing for contested skies, disrupted evacuations, and thousands of temporary battlefield burials.\n\nNOW CONSIDER THE BIGGER PICTURE.\n\nWe've also tracked Q's references to a potential \"scare event,\" the emergency broadcast language in Drop 34, and the 11.3/11.4 references throughout the drops.\n\nMAJOR EVENT NARRATIVE SEEDING — the documented developments continue accumulating.\n\nGovernments discussing emergency stockpiles.\n\nWarnings about cyberattacks and infrastructure disruption.\n\nExpanded military preparedness.\n\nAnd now the Army rehearsing battlefield burials on a scale not needed since Korea.\n\nAre we witnessing the buildup of narratives that could precede a much larger event?\n\nAll we can do is watch what happens.\n\nFuture proves past? We'll see.\n\n[https://www.armytimes.com/news/your-army/2026/10/26/army-practices-digging-temporary-battlefield-graves/](https://www.armytimes.com/news/your-army/2026/10/26/army-practices-digging-temporary-battlefield-graves/)\n\n🇺🇸🟨🇺🇸",
